  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Viasat has $322M in contract obligations for FY2026 to date. Viasat won 123 awards this fiscal year, with an average award size of $2.6M, and obligations are up 17.7% year over year. Viasat received the largest share of obligations from the Department of Defense, which obligated $201M, followed by the General Services Administration, which obligated $119M. Obligations by fiscal year show a multi-year pattern: FY21 $484M, FY22 $561M, FY23 $527M, FY24 $341M, FY25 $273M, and FY26 $322M. Viasat’s biggest NAICS markets are Other Communications Equipment Manufacturing with $189M and Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing with $75M. Viasat also has work in Radio and Television Broadcasting and Wireless Communications Equipment Manufacturing with $26.2M, Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences with $12.6M, and Engineering Services with $8M. Smaller NAICS entries include Satellite Telecommunications with $7.8M, Computer Terminal and Other Computer Peripheral Equipment Manufacturing with $1.8M, and other categories down to Wired Telecommunications Carriers with $2.5K.",
    "sections": [
