        "heading": "What is Viasat’s current federal contracting footprint?",
        "body": "Viasat has $322M in obligations in FY2026 to date and 123 awards, with an average award size of $2.6M. Viasat’s obligations are up 17.7% year over year. Viasat’s fiscal-year obligations have varied: FY21 $484M, FY22 $561M, FY23 $527M, FY24 $341M, and FY25 $273M. Viasat’s largest buying agencies are the Department of Defense with $201M and the General Services Administration with $119M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Where does Viasat sell most work inside the federal government?",
        "body": "Viasat sells most work to the Department of Defense, which obligated $201M. Viasat also sells significant work to the General Services Administration, which obligated $119M, and to smaller buyers such as the Department of Homeland Security with $1.4M and NASA with $346K. Viasat’s top industrial markets are Other Communications Equipment Manufacturing with $189M and Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing with $75M."
